chromium-seccomp.json is the Chromium user-namespace seccomp profile distributed
by Microsoft Playwright under Apache-2.0.
Source: https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/ae935a43d9e376e4759548f6b3c6905c7b282333/utils/docker/seccomp_profile.json
SHA-256: cc3e61cabda6bbc1e53e54d27ba4d55a9d3be829b6dd1a596f4a7b31b1cc7849
License: https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/main/LICENSE
The profile extends Docker's default syscall set with user-namespace operations
needed by Chromium's sandbox. It is installed only on browser workers.

Local change: explicitly allow chroot in addition to the upstream profile. Docker
otherwise drops that syscall when all container capabilities are dropped, including
inside Chromium's newly created user namespace. The outer process remains non-root
with all capabilities dropped and no-new-privileges; the Chromium sandbox stays on.
Validated with the amd64 worker image on local Docker Desktop, Chromium158.0.8127.18.
